      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: Revenues exceed analysts expectations while EPS lags behind",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹11.73 (up from ₹8.17 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹30.4b (up 12% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹1.61b (up 43% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 5.3% (up from 4.1% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue exceeded analyst estimates by 1.1%. Earnings per share (EPS) missed analyst estimates by 8.3%. Revenue is forecast to grow 7.9% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, compared to a 13% growth forecast for the Consumer Durables industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has fallen by 29% per year but the company’s share price has only fallen by 8% per year, which means it has not declined as severely as earnings.",
